# Visual Decision Rules

## Case 1 — No Visual Required

If the question is based on:

* Definitions
* Establishment year
* Appointment or removal procedures
* Legal status
* Headquarters
* One-line factual information
* Acts establishing institutions

Then:

* Do NOT generate a visual.

---

## Case 2 — Selective Visual Required

Generate visuals only when they significantly improve understanding.

Examples:

* Regulatory body comparison
* Statutory vs Constitutional vs Regulatory vs Quasi-Judicial bodies
* LPG reforms timeline
* Institutional hierarchy
* Public sector reforms
* Tribunal appellate structure
* Administrative reform process

---

## Case 3 — Visual-Intensive Concepts

Generate visuals whenever they clearly improve learning.

Examples:

* Comparison tables
* Governance flow visuals
* Tribunal hierarchy
* Regulatory ecosystem
* Administrative reform workflow
* Institutional classification

Never generate visuals merely to satisfy a percentage.

